A human decision is needed on work item `sample/08` — **Synth body**. Everything needed to
decide is in this issue.

How to reply: comment from your own account with the board id of this item and the chosen option,
as `sample/08: <option>` (for example `sample/08: 1`); the comment is the decision
record. Name the board id in your own words — a bare option number or a one-word "approved"
is not accepted as a ruling when the item later moves on the board. Then close the issue.

## Context

Confirm the cost of the change.

It is cheaper.

Risk answers: none. Effort: M.

## Options

1. **Approve as briefed** — the work proceeds and lands exactly as described above; your approval is the human gate it is waiting on.
2. **Approve with changes** — state the changes as a comment on this issue; the work is re-dispatched with them folded in before it lands.
3. **Hold / reject** — state why as a comment; the item is parked and cannot advance past its human gate.

Default if no answer: none — the gate blocks until answered.
